.el .ds Aq '
.TH dalgona 1  "dalgona 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
dalgona \- Run the dal coding agent.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdalgona\fR [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-print\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\-last\-message\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-continue\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-resume\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-thinking\fR] [\fB\-\-approval\fR] [\fB\-\-sandbox\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-screen\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-cd\fR] [\fB\-\-connect\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the dal coding agent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-print\fR
Print the assistant response and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON result object or error object; exit 1 on error.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\-last\-message\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the last assistant message to FILE after a successful run.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-continue\fR
Continue the newest session in this workspace.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-resume\fR [\fI<RESUME>\fR]
Resume a session by id or name, or open the session picker.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name the session.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Use model ID for this run. ID may name a provider route, an alias, a registered synthetic model, or a dalgon mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Harness mode for this run: normal, eval\-first, or eval\-only. The ids dalgon/normal, dalgon/eval\-first, and dalgon/eval\-only in \-\-model select the same modes.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
normal
.IP \(bu 2
eval\-first
.IP \(bu 2
eval\-only
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-thinking\fR \fI<THINKING>\fR
Set the provider reasoning level.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
off
.IP \(bu 2
minimal
.IP \(bu 2
low
.IP \(bu 2
medium
.IP \(bu 2
high
.IP \(bu 2
xhigh
.IP \(bu 2
max
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-approval\fR \fI<APPROVAL>\fR
Approval policy for patch and exec tool calls: ask, edits, or all. ask asks in the UI and denies calls in headless runs. edits approves edit calls without asking and asks for exec. all approves every call; use it only inside an external sandbox.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
ask
.IP \(bu 2
edits
.IP \(bu 2
all
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-sandbox\fR
Enable the configured sandbox.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-session\fR
Do not persist this session.
.TP
\fB\-\-screen\fR \fI<SCREEN>\fR
Select the terminal screen mode.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
inline
.IP \(bu 2
fullscreen
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Select terminal color behavior.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-cd\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Use DIR as the workspace without changing the process working directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
Connect to a remote dalgon host and run the interactive terminal UI. Without this option, dalgon uses a host in this process.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read the bearer token from FILE; it is sent only to non\-loopback WebSocket endpoints. No token file is inferred.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPROMPT\fR]
Attach text, image, or piped standard\-input content to the first user message.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
dalgona\-login(1)
Sign in to a provider or inspect sign\-in state.
.TP
dalgona\-logout(1)
Sign out from a provider.
.TP
dalgona\-models(1)
List models and show built\-in prices, price source, and fetch date when available.
.TP
dalgona\-docs(1)
Read a dalgon documentation page.
.TP
dalgona\-serve(1)
Start the local control server or create its token.
.TP
dalgona\-rpc(1)
Serve the JSON\-RPC protocol on standard input and output.
.TP
dalgona\-acp(1)
Serve the Agent Client Protocol on standard input and output.
.TP
dalgona\-app\-server(1)
Serve the Codex app\-server protocol on standard input and output.
.TP
dalgona\-completion(1)
Generate shell completion scripts.
.TP
dalgona\-plugin(1)
Manage configured plugin grants.
.TP
dalgona\-rules(1)
Inspect or test stream rules.
.TP
dalgona\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
